course: dictionary
lesson: 15524
title: Substrate: what things grow and live on
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A substrate is the surface or material that something grows on or lives on. Think of the soil under a plant, or the sand and rock at the bottom of a rock pool. «The seaweed grows on the rock, so the rock is its substrate.»
explain: Scientists use the word in another way too. In chemistry and biology, a substrate is the substance that an enzyme acts on and changes. «Enzymes break down substrates.» The enzyme is the worker, and the substrate is the thing it works on.
explain: To find the meaning, read the words around it. If something grows on it, lives on it, or is changed by something else, it may be a substrate. Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A substrate is the surface or material that something grows on or lives on.
fact: Soil, sand, rock and the gravel in a fish tank can all be substrates.
fact: In chemistry and biology, a substrate is the substance that an enzyme acts on and changes.
fact: In technology, a substrate is a base layer that something else is built on, such as the material under a computer chip.
fact: Reptile and fish owners choose a safe substrate for their tank, because the animals live on it every day.
exercise: In a rock pool, what is the substrate? | The fish swimming above | *The sand and rock at the bottom | The sunlight on the water
exercise: «Enzymes break down substrates.» What is a substrate in this sentence? | A tiny animal | The water the enzyme floats in | The enzyme itself | *The substance an enzyme acts on and changes
exercise: «Ella chose a safe substrate for her gecko's tank.» What is the substrate for? | For the lamp to stand on | For the gecko to fly | For the computer in the room | *For the gecko to live on
test: Which can be the substrate for a plant? | The bright lamp in the room | Soil | *Gravel | The sky above it
test: What is the base layer under a computer chip called? | A pond | An enzyme | *A substrate | A habitat
exam: «The moss grows on the stone, so the stone is its ___.» Which word fits best? | gravel | enzyme | *substrate | habitat
